# Firebase web configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (which is gitignored) and paste in the values
# from the Firebase console: Project settings -> Your apps -> the web app ->
# "SDK setup and configuration".
#
# These are NOT secrets. Google documents the web config as public, and it
# necessarily ships inside the JavaScript bundle where anyone can read it. What
# protects the data is `firestore.rules`, not the obscurity of these values.
#
# They are kept out of the repository anyway for two practical reasons:
#   1. The API key matches gitleaks' Google-API-key pattern, so committing it
#      reddens the secret scan in CI — and this project's policy
#      (.gitleaks.toml) is that allowlisting a credential pattern is never the
#      fix.
#   2. It keeps a fork pointed at its own project instead of writing into this
#      one.
#
# Leaving them unset is supported: the app builds, starts, and runs its tests,
# and the sign-in screen explains that no backend is configured.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
